clean_summary:
Zach Mueller criticizes slop as high-quality exposition that lacks clarity and disrespects the reader's time. A suggested approach is to ask models directly, with your own context and prompts.

@jacobpeake shares a new long-form blog post covering leading AI chip architectures like NVIDIA, AMD, TPUs, Trainium, Cerebras, and Groq, focusing on architecture, scaling, and software stacks. It aims to build intuition about their trade-offs.

The linked URLs include a guide on how to scale your model, GPU programming resources, tile primitives for kernels, and an overview of AI chip architectures by Jacob Peake.
